<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14975" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρήγω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ξω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
					12.5D.
				</span></i>
			, etc.:—<i>aid, succour,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.363
				</span></i>
			, al. (never in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>); in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always, <i>succour in war,</i> freq. c. dat. pers. et
			modi, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχῃ Τρώεσσιν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.521
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				5.507
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμοσσον ἦ μέν μοι . . ἔπεσιν καὶ
					χερσὶν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.77
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>help, succour,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέχει Ἀλκμήνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					1.49
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεότατι ἀ. θράσος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>P.</u>
					2.63
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θνητοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					269
				</span></i>
			, etc.; in mock Trag. passages of Com., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναῖκες, οὐκ ἀρήξετ᾽;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					696
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pl.</u>
				476
			</span></i>: rare in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Hecat.
				30J.
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ναυτικὸς τῷ πεζῷ ἀρήξει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.236
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς φίλοις ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					1.5.13
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. σὺν ὅπλοις τῇ χώρᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Oec.</u>
					5.7
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be good for</i> a patient or his case, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prorrh.</u>
				2.30
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Acut.</u>
				65
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> impers., c.
				inf., <i>it is good</i> or <i>fit,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρειν ἀρήγει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					2.94
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιγᾶν ἀρήγει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					571
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc. rei,
				<i>ward off, prevent,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄλεθρον</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Batr.
				279
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρηξον . . ἅλωσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					119
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τινί τι</span>
			<i>ward off from</i> one, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόνον τέκνοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					1275
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tr.</u>
				777
			</span></i>. (Perh. cognate with Lat. <i>rēx,</i> Skt.
				<i>rā´jati</i> 'rule'.)</div>
